.policy "ruff-isc001-single-line-implicit-string-concatenation" revision 1
.guests off
.description "Join string literals that are implicitly concatenated on one line into a single literal; the split adds nothing and may hide a forgotten comma."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"
// Generated from today's JSON by docs/rule-syntax/site/translate.py. Display only: not compiled or run.

// ISC001(n): findings from clauses `pairs-from-first-literal`, `pairs-from-second-literal`, which say the same.
// Each rule is one way a JSON `rule` can match.
// Columns after `at` are the metavariables the JSON's message, anchor or `each` names: one finding per distinct row.
.violation ISC001(at: node, p: node) "Merge these adjacent literals into one string, escaping any braces or quotes the merge exposes; if they were meant as separate items, add the missing comma instead."
    suppress noqa "ISC001"
